  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The addition polymerisation of acrylonitrile in presence of a peroxide catalyst leads to the formation of polyacrylonitrile. The commercial name of polyacrylonitrile is orlon (acrilan). That is, it is used as a substitute for wool in making commercial fibres as orlon or acrilan.&nbsp;</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/ffff4193-687e-4fa5-9b67-ac8c70595f55.png\" style=\"width: 454px; height: 99px;\" /></p></blockquote>",
